    <h1>🍽️ Horse Nutrition Overview</h1>
    <p>Good nutrition is the foundation of a healthy horse. What a horse eats affects its energy, coat condition, mood, and lifespan.</p>

    <h2>🌿 The Basics of What Horses Eat</h2>
    <p>Horses are herbivores designed for small, frequent meals. In the wild, horses graze for 16–20 hours a day!</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Forage (hay/grass):</strong> Should make up 60–100% of the diet</li>
        <li><strong>Concentrates (grains):</strong> Only needed for high energy demands</li>
        <li><strong>Supplements:</strong> Vitamins and minerals to fill nutritional gaps</li>
        <li><strong>Water:</strong> The most important nutrient — always available</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>⚖️ How Much Should a Horse Eat?</h2>
    <p>A horse should eat approximately <strong>1.5–2% of its body weight</strong> in dry feed per day.</p>

