    <h2>🔑 Key Nutritional Needs</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Energy:</strong> From carbohydrates and fats in forage and grains</li>
        <li><strong>Protein:</strong> Important for muscle growth and repair</li>
        <li><strong>Fiber:</strong> Essential for healthy digestion — prevents colic</li>
        <li><strong>Vitamins:</strong> A, D, E, and B-complex</li>
        <li><strong>Minerals:</strong> Calcium, phosphorus, salt, magnesium</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>⚠️ Common Feeding Mistakes</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Too much grain and not enough hay</li>
        <li>Sudden diet changes — always transition over 1–2 weeks</li>
        <li>Feeding on the ground in dirty areas</li>
        <li>Skipping water or providing dirty water</li>
    </ul>

